  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c8000.html",
  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 8004.07 Business Entity License",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 8004.07 Business Entity License.\n\n(a) A license shall be issued to any business entity, as defined in Saf-C 8002.01, engaged in the servicing, repair, installation or demolition of fuel gas piping systems, fuel gas utilization systems and fuel gas appliances, including the installation, combustion air supply and venting of fuel gas utilization equipment using liquefied propane gas or natural gas.\n\n(b) No license shall be issued to any business entity that does not show proof of good standing with the NH secretary of state’s office.\n\n(c) Each business entity shall provide a responsible managing employee, as defined in Saf-C 8002.19, to represent the business entity as the licensee of record.\n\n(d) Each responsible managing employee shall:\n\n(1) Be the business entity’s principle officer or other employee who is an active participant in the business;\n\n(2) Possess a current and valid liquefied propane gas service technician license or a natural gas service technician license; and\n\n(3) Agree to act on behalf of the business entity as the licensee of record.\n\n(e) The business entity shall notify the state fire marshal’s office within 30 days of the death or termination of a responsible managing employee’s status.\n\nSource. #9542, eff 9-10-09",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c8000.html"
}
